WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.160
- We've been celebrating
World Teachers' Day

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.230
with an audience full of educators.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.715
I wanna close out with one
more story for our teachers.

00:00:07.715 --> 00:00:08.848
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:08.848 --> 00:00:11.730
(upbeat music sting)

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.130
More than 90% of teachers
say they have to dig

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.260
into their own pockets to cover the cost

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.480
of school supplies in their classrooms.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.660
One non-profit in North Carolina
is alleviating that burden

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.150
on teachers in disadvantaged communities.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.090
For 20 years, Classroom
Central has run a shop

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:31.410
where teachers can come and
load up on supplies for free.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.210
We have the founding executive director

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.200
on the line right now.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.052
Everybody say hello to Karen.

00:00:36.052 --> 00:00:38.520
(audience cheering)

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.563
Hi, Karen.

00:00:39.563 --> 00:00:40.740
- Hey, Kelly.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.270
- Oh my God, this is so cool.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.100
So, the teachers still get to shop,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.720
they just don't have to pay, right?

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.746
- That's right. So, we're set up just like

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:50.910
any other retail operation would be.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.540
The only difference is we
don't have any cash registers.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.080
Everything is available
100% free of charge.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.370
And as you can imagine,
teachers get really excited-

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.203
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:03.203 --> 00:01:06.660
- About the opportunity
to come and shop with us.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.860
Our free store is stocked

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.170
with everything that you can imagine.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.330
Books, and backpacks,

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:16.231
and incentives to motivate
and reward students.

00:01:16.231 --> 00:01:19.170
And, of course, we have
all the basic supplies

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:22.350
like pencils, and
crayons, and glue sticks.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.240
Really, everything that you can imagine

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.330
having in a backpack or a classroom.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.670
- This is just the coolest
thing ever, you have no idea.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.260
Like my mother really could have used this

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.130
'cause we didn't have money

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.980
and she used to use ours that
we didn't have to do that.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.470
And- and that's what a
lot of you probably do

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.520
and it's a really cool thing.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.860
So where do you get the supplies from?

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.760
- Yeah, so most of the
supplies are donated through-

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.720
we have supply drives that
take place in the summer,

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.110
but we also have just
organizations that are collecting

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.970
for us year-round,

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.480
businesses that make or manufacture goods

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.580
that are giving those to us

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.380
periodically throughout the year.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.500
And we also, since we're a nonprofit,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.290
we have folks that
contribute to us financially

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:11.100
and we use a portion of that
money to go out and buy things.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.770
I mean, we can't have a
free school supply store

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:14.940
if we don't have pencils.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.370
So oftentimes, when we're running low,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.250
we'll go and we'll actually
buy those materials.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.650
And so, it's really because
of our amazing community

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.220
that has been supporting
us for almost 20 years-

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.053
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:27.907
- That we've been able to give away

00:02:27.907 --> 00:02:31.140
$80 million worth of free school supplies.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:32.218
- Wow.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.570
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.460
- Oh my God, congratulations.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.950
That's- that's incredible. All
those people you're helping.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.570
Thank you so much, Karen.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.588
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:41.588 --> 00:02:42.460
(ding)

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:43.293
And that's not all,

00:02:43.293 --> 00:02:44.940
our season-long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.830
makers of Frixion, the go-to erasable pen

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:47.880
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.280
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.900
just like Classroom Central,

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.396
so they're giving your
not-for-profit $1,000.

00:02:55.396 --> 00:02:57.884
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:02:57.884 --> 00:02:58.717
- Thank you so much.

00:02:58.717 --> 00:03:00.120
- Thank you.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.800
Thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.414
Dr. Jill Biden, LeVar
Burton, Kirsten, and Justin,

00:03:05.414 --> 00:03:07.140
and just a huge thank you

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.740
to each and every teacher
here and watching at home.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.480
I know some days get really tough,

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.080
but you are doing angels'
work and you are appreciated.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.910
Trust. Have a great day y'all.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.127
And if it's not, try and change it.

